Given todo (todo items with invalid or misleading syntax);
x   .    1    .    2    .    3    .    4    .    5    .    6    .    7    .    8  L01
x 345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890  L02
X Done tasks must start with a lowercase x then space                             L03
xDone tasks must start with a lowercase x then space                              L04
XDone tasks must start with a lowercase x then space                              L05
(a) Priority must start with an uppercase letter in rounds followed by space      L06
(A)Priority must start with an uppercase letter in rounds followed by space       L07
A  Priority must start with an uppercase letter in rounds followed by space       L08
a  Priority must start with an uppercase letter in rounds followed by space       L09
Priority (A) must start with an uppercase letter in rounds followed by space      L10
due:2050-01-01 keys are valid on the start of the line                            L11
due:2010-01-01 overdue dates are valid on the start of the line                   L12
2010-01-01 dates are valid on the start of the line                               L13
x   .    1    .    2    .    3    .    4    .    5    .    6    .    7    .    8  L14
x 345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890  L15
Invalid dates 17-10-05 20100101 01-01-2010 2010/01/01 10/01/01 2010-01-01-2010    L16
@Contexts are valid on the start of the line                                      L17
+Projects are valid on the start of the line                                      L18
The key: syntax must be followed by a value, same for due:                        L19
due: syntax must be a whole word notdue:2010-01-01 pro@jects and con+texts also   L20
x 345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890  L21
x   .    1    .    2    .    3    .    4    .    5    .    6    .    7    .    8  L22
Execute (Syntax for invalid or misleading tasks):
  " Invalid done or priority: still inbox, not a formulated task
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 3,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 4,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 5,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 6,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 7,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 8,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt( 9,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(10,  1)
  " Valid keys and dates at start of line
  AssertEqual 'TodoKey',          SyntaxAt(11,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoDate',         SyntaxAt(11,  5)
  AssertEqual 'TodoOverDueDate',  SyntaxAt(12,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoDate',         SyntaxAt(13,  1)
  " Invalid date formats.
  " FIXME: Not all cases are tested, not sure how strict to be
  " AssertEqual '',                 SyntaxAt(16, 15)  " FIXME
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 24)
  " AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 33)  " FIXME
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 42)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 44)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 55)
  " AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 64)  " FIXME
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(16, 78)
  " Contexts and projects on the start of a line (valid)
  AssertEqual 'TodoContext',      SyntaxAt(17,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoProject',      SyntaxAt(18,  1)
  " Invalid keys, etc
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(19,  5)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(19, 55)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(20,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoKey',          SyntaxAt(20, 34)
  AssertEqual 'TodoDate',         SyntaxAt(20, 41)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(20, 55)
  AssertEqual 'TodoInbox',        SyntaxAt(20, 69)
Do (Insert a task due today):
  OTask due-\<BS>:\<C-R>=strftime("%Y-%m-%d")\<CR> today\<C-O>
Then (Syntax for task due today):
  Log getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoDueToday', SyntaxAt(1, 12)
Execute (Default role highlight links):
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityA
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Constant', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityAMark
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Todo', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityB
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Function', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityC
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Type', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityZ
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Type', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoDone
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Comment', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  AssertEqual '1', synIDattr(hlID('TodoInbox'), 'italic', 'gui')
  AssertEqual '1', synIDattr(hlID('TodoInbox'), 'underline', 'gui')
  AssertEqual '#000000', tolower(synIDattr(hlID('TodoActive'), 'fg#', 'gui'))
  AssertEqual '#d7ff00', tolower(synIDattr(hlID('TodoActive'), 'bg#', 'gui'))
  let g:Todo_txt_highlight = {'B': 'Statement', 'InboxItalic': 0, 'Active': 'Error'}
  call todo#ApplyHighlight()
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityB
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Statement', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoInbox
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Underlined', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoActive
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Error', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  unlet g:Todo_txt_highlight
  call todo#ApplyHighlight()
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPriorityB
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Function', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  AssertEqual '#000000', tolower(synIDattr(hlID('TodoActive'), 'fg#', 'gui'))
  AssertEqual '#d7ff00', tolower(synIDattr(hlID('TodoActive'), 'bg#', 'gui'))
  unlet g:todo_hi
Given todo (Periodic stubs are parked, not formulated);
(P) Pay the internet +home every:1m last:2026-09-01 rid:a1b2
2026-09-01 (P) Book a dentist +health show:2026-10-14
(P) Water the flowers +garden active:1
x 2026-09-30 (P) Finished stub
(C) A formulated task +home
(O) The priority next to P
Execute (Syntax for a (P) stub):
  " The whole line is one dim group: tags, dates and projects stay inside it
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(1,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(1,  5)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(1, 22)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(1, 42)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(1, 57)
Execute (A creation date in front of a stub):
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(2,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(2, 12)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPeriodic',   SyntaxAt(2, 31)
Execute (active:1 and x still win over a stub):
  AssertEqual 'TodoActive',     SyntaxAt(3,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoActive',     SyntaxAt(3, 31)
  AssertEqual 'TodoDone',       SyntaxAt(4,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoDone',       SyntaxAt(4, 14)
Execute (The priorities around P are untouched):
  AssertEqual 'TodoPriorityC',  SyntaxAt(5,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPriorityC',  SyntaxAt(5,  5)
  " A formulated task keeps its inner items, a stub does not
  AssertEqual 'TodoProject',    SyntaxAt(5, 22)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPriorityO',  SyntaxAt(6,  1)
  AssertEqual 'TodoPriorityO',  SyntaxAt(6,  5)
Execute (Periodic role highlight):
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPeriodic
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Comment', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  " P left the (A)-(Z) loop, so the Other role does not define it either
  AssertEqual 0, hlexists('TodoPriorityP')
  let g:Todo_txt_highlight = {'Periodic': 'Statement'}
  call todo#ApplyHighlight()
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPeriodic
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Statement', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  unlet g:Todo_txt_highlight
  call todo#ApplyHighlight()
  redir => g:todo_hi
  silent highlight TodoPeriodic
  redir END
  AssertEqual 'Comment', matchstr(g:todo_hi, 'links to \zs\S\+')
  unlet g:todo_hi

