" function todo#Sort(type) and todo#HierarchicalSort() {{{2

" Both sorts repoint g:Todo_fold_char at what they sorted on, folding follows
" the last sort. Put it back, the tests below and above rely on 'x'.
Before:
  let g:todo_fold_char_saved = g:Todo_fold_char
After:
  let g:Todo_fold_char = g:todo_fold_char_saved
  unlet g:todo_fold_char_saved
Given todo (Stubs scattered among the tasks):
  (B) Pay the internet +home rid:a1b2
  Inbox note +home
  (P) Water the flowers +garden every:1m rid:b2c3
  (A) Control the repair +home
  (P) Book a dentist +health show:2026-10-14
  (C) Read the report +work
  x 2026-09-01 Old done task +home
Execute (Sort the tasks):
  " <LocalLeader>s is what the user presses, but \s is a prefix of \sc, \s@,
  " \s+ and \sd, so a Do block leaves Vim waiting for the rest of the mapping
  " and the keys leak into the next test. The calls below are what it runs.
  AssertEqual ':call todo#Sort("")<CR>', maparg('\s', 'n')
  AssertEqual ':call todo#Sort("@")<CR>', maparg('\s@', 'n')
  call todo#Sort('')
Expect todo (Stubs collected at the tail of the active tasks):
  (A) Control the repair +home
  (B) Pay the internet +home rid:a1b2
  (C) Read the report +work
  Inbox note +home
  (P) Water the flowers +garden every:1m rid:b2c3
  (P) Book a dentist +health show:2026-10-14
  x 2026-09-01 Old done task +home

